# Upgrade limits stamped into every release file as min_upgrade_from and schema_floor
# (docs/plan/07-server-install-update.md sections 2 and 6.3), as xWriter's
# tools/release/compat.env. Sourced by build.sh.
#
# MIN_UPGRADE_FROM is the oldest installed version that this release can update from
# directly; xdesign update refuses older installations, which must first update to an
# intermediate release. Raise it when this release relies on work that only a release newer
# than MIN_UPGRADE_FROM did, for example a data step whose follow-up ships now.
#
# SCHEMA_FLOOR is the oldest release that runs on the database schema this release's
# migrations create. Raise it to this release's version when a migration changes the schema
# in a way older releases cannot read: going back below it then needs the backup the update
# took.
#
# Both are X.Y.Z and never newer than the release itself (build.sh checks it).
#
# 0.3.0 (lead, 2026-11-23): M14 removes users.email and the invite and reset tables
# (migrations 0011 and 0012, docs/plan/18 section 3.2), which 0.2.0 reads at sign-in; the owner's
# server runs 0.2.0, so the first release with M14 is 0.3.0 or newer.
MIN_UPGRADE_FROM=0.0.0
SCHEMA_FLOOR=0.3.0
